# WebAPI controllers

- Controllers derive from `BaseController` and only build a request, send it with `Mediator.Send` and return the
  response. No business logic, validation or data access here.
- One controller per feature, named `<PluralEntity>Controller`, routed as `api/[controller]`.
- Endpoints of generated commands and queries are added by nArchGen; keep their shape when adding one by hand:
  `[FromBody]` commands, `[FromQuery]` queries and `PageRequest`, `[FromRoute]` ids.
- Do not catch exceptions here: the exception middleware (`ConfigureCustomExceptionMiddleware` in `Program.cs`) turns
  business, validation and authorization exceptions into responses. The starter enables it only in the Production
  environment; check `Program.cs` before relying on it in other environments.
